PROCESS ANALYSIS

1. PURPOSE

The purpose of this process analysis is to understand the current employee transportation process, identify operational gaps and define an improved To-Be process.


2. AS-IS PROCESS

Employee Transportation Request
↓
Shuttle Booking
↓
Demand Consolidation
↓
Capacity Planning
↓
Route Planning
↓
Vehicle / Vendor Assignment
↓
Trip Execution
↓
Issue Handling
↓
Performance Review
↓
Management Decision


3. AS-IS PAIN POINTS

• Limited visibility of employee demand
• Manual demand consolidation
• Vehicle capacity mismatch
• Inefficient routes
• Difficult delay tracking
• Poor cancellation analysis
• Limited vendor performance visibility
• Fragmented KPI reporting


4. TO-BE PROCESS

Employee Booking
↓
Data Validation
↓
Demand Analysis
↓
Capacity Planning
↓
Route Review
↓
Vendor Planning
↓
Trip Execution
↓
Incident Capture
↓
KPI Dashboard
↓
Continuous Improvement

![image alt](https://github.com/komalkumari2322001-netizen/employee-commute-shuttle-optimization/blob/6c23fd42cf202606c550481b700f64abc10fa6b6/flow%20chart.png).

5. KEY PROCESS IMPROVEMENTS

• Centralized demand analysis
• Demand-based capacity planning
• Improved route planning
• Standardized incident tracking
• Centralized KPI dashboard
• Better vendor performance monitoring
• Data-driven decision making


6. PROCESS KPIs

• Vehicle Utilization %
• Route Utilization %
• Average Waiting Time
• Average Delay
• On-Time Performance %
• Cancellation Rate
• Cost per Trip


7. BA CONCLUSION

The proposed To-Be process improves transportation visibility, capacity planning, route efficiency and KPI monitoring.

It enables management to identify operational problems and take data-driven decisions to improve employee commute experience and transportation efficiency.
